                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I think it’s important to note that if you’re reading this, while I will keep this review brief and spoiler-free, the way I experienced this tale is the only way I can imagine it being most optimal. That would be blind, spoiler-free w little to no expectations. \n\nWith that being said, I dove into this game w no context whatsoever. I enjoy going into things as blind as possible, which is hard to avoid being online or receiving recommendations on whatever material is considered to be among the “best” of its medium. I had seen this game/novel recommended to me several times as I perused steam’s shop, but what had actually convinced me to pull the trigger was listening to a song titled “Fata Morgana” by the artist “Aeriu Ika”. \n\nLight spoilers ahead, but even what lied behind the first door alone had gripped me. You can surmise my pleasure when I realized I had barely even scratched the surface. That this tale would only proceed to sink its claws further and further in me until I couldn’t pull away, even if I’d wanted to. I was hooked. \n\nI wouldn’t say I’m really a visual novel enthusiast. A ton of the titles intrigue me, but I’m really easy to intrigue, and after that, pretty easy to please, but I’m not particularly a fan of reading. I know this medium provides the visual and audio aids to help the process feel less like a chore, but even without them, I believe this story would have kept me captivated the entire way. That’s not to downplay the incredible artwork and soundtrack this game has to offer though. I don’t think any one element of this game is more valuable than the other, but I think it’s important to highlight and distinguish that while they work together to create this amazing experience, they are each independently outstanding. \n\nI generally wait a bit after finishing something before I dive into the next. Games, series, whatever form that may take, but I didn’t hesitate to begin requiem the following day upon completing Fata Morgana. I’ve only just begun that, but it’s been just as pleasant an experience as I’ve had w this game. \n\nI’m grateful to have experienced this story, and I believe what I’ve walked away w from it will shape me to lead a more fulfilling life. Crazy to suggest something like that after sitting down dedicating dozens of hours to a game in only a few sittings, BUT, I do believe it to be true. \n\nI give no rating, because I rate solely off how something makes me feel, and because of that, I rate everything ridiculously high. So my rating doesn’t mean all that much. I’m not a critic, by any means. With that being said, I do strongly recommend playing/reading this game. At whatever pace you please. I doubt one could walk away from this experience feeling regret for having gone through it.",
